# shellcheck shell=bash
#
# WHAT A RELEASE COMMIT HOLDS: the files `bin/devbin build release` stamps, and
# the classifier for the views it folds in beside them. Sourced by the release
# driver, which writes that commit, and by `int prepush`, which recognises it:
# the commit a cut makes after its candidate passed the Linux preflight is
# covered by that preflight only while it holds nothing else (hv's ruling,
# 2026-10-23, read by vc under hv's pen). Moved here from the driver so the
# commit the driver writes and the commit the gate accepts are one definition.

# The config and the native pair, named once for the driver's own reads and
# for the list below.
CONFIG_REL="intent/.config/config.json"
NATIVE_MANIFEST_REL="native/rust/Cargo.toml"
NATIVE_LOCK_REL="native/rust/Cargo.lock"

# The sidecars the driver owns end to end: it writes them, stages them, and
# refuses to tag if anything else is left dirty. ONE list, read by the detect
# step and the commit step alike, so the two cannot disagree about what a
# release commit contains.
#
# `native/rust/Cargo.toml` carries `[workspace.package] version`, every crate
# inherits it with `version.workspace = true`, and both binaries compile their
# own version string from `env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")`. So the workspace version
# IS the v3 product's version -- the number on `intent --version` and on the
# page intentd serves -- and the lockfile records it per member, so the two must
# move together.
#
# THIS WAS CONDITIONAL ON A 3.x TARGET AND THE CONDITION IS NOW UNREACHABLE, so
# it is deleted rather than left as a guard that reads as live. Its own comment
# predicted the retirement -- "once 2.x stops being cut there is no other arm" --
# and what retired it is not a judgement call: `semver_gt "$TARGET" "$CURRENT"`
# in the driver aborts anything not GREATER than the current version, and the
# current version is a 3.x. A 2.x target cannot reach this line to be excluded
# by it.
#
# The hazard the condition guarded is real and has simply moved upstream:
# stamping `2.19.1` into the Rust workspace would make the next v3 build
# announce itself as a v2. If 2.x is ever cut again it will be from a branch
# whose VERSION is a 2.x, where `semver_gt` admits it -- and the driver will
# need the arm back. That is a deliberate condition to restore at that point,
# not a silent behaviour to rediscover.
#
# THE NATIVE PAIR WAS AN APPEND TO THIS LIST UNTIL 2026-09-11, which made the
# append a second home for the list the comment above says there is one of
# (vc, AC-00.6). Folded into the one declaration; the set is unchanged.
# `schema` is a DIRECTORY entry on purpose: the faces are generated, so a face
# added to a future release joins the commit without this list being edited.
SIDECAR_FILES="VERSION CHANGELOG.md AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md $CONFIG_REL $NATIVE_MANIFEST_REL $NATIVE_LOCK_REL schema"

# `footer_only` reads one file's `git diff -U0` on stdin and exits 0 when every
# changed line is the generated footer, `_Generated by Intent vX ...` (the major
# alone since 2026-09-25) or the older `vX.Y.Z ...`, and 1 otherwise, including
# when nothing changed at all. The driver's re-render fold trusts it (issue
# 0464), and so does `release_stamp_only` below.
#
# It counts only lines INSIDE a hunk. It used to select changed lines with
# `^[-+][^-+]`, which also skipped every changed line whose own text starts with
# `-` or `+`: a markdown bullet reads `-- item` or `+- item` in a diff, and a
# removed or added blank line reads `-` or `+` alone. A view whose only real
# change was a bullet was classed footer-only and folded into the release
# commit under the release message. Tracking the hunk is what tells a
# `--- a/<path>` file header from a removed line reading `-- ...`.
footer_only() {
  awk '
    /^diff --git / { in_hunk = 0; next }
    /^@@ / { in_hunk = 1; next }
    !in_hunk { next }
    /^[-+]/ {
      changed++
      if ($0 !~ /^[-+]_Generated by Intent v[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+)? /) other = 1
    }
    END { exit (changed > 0 && !other) ? 0 : 1 }
  '
}

# release_stamp_only <root> <parent> <commit> -- exit 0 when <commit> changes,
# against <parent>, something and nothing but what the driver's release commit
# holds: the SIDECAR_FILES (a directory entry covers its tree) and views whose
# change is their footer alone. 1 otherwise, and 1 when git cannot answer.
#
# KNOWN BY ITS DIFF, NEVER BY ITS TAG OR ITS MESSAGE (vc, 2026-10-23): a tag is
# a name and the diff is the fact, so nothing depends on who made the tag.
release_stamp_only() {
  local root=$1 parent=$2 commit=$3 paths path entry hit any=0 diff
  paths="$(git -C "$root" diff --name-only "$parent" "$commit")" || return 1
  while IFS= read -r path; do
    [ -n "$path" ] || continue
    any=1
    hit=0
    for entry in $SIDECAR_FILES; do
      case "$path" in "$entry" | "$entry"/*) hit=1 && break ;; esac
    done
    [ "$hit" -eq 1 ] && continue
    diff="$(git -C "$root" diff -U0 "$parent" "$commit" -- "$path")" || return 1
    printf '%s\n' "$diff" | footer_only || return 1
  done <<<"$paths"
  [ "$any" -eq 1 ]
}
